---
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/site-path';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LiveLine from '../../examples/line/app';
import { lineSources } from '../../lib/line-sources';
---
<Layout title="Live line example — Foldkit Viz">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/')}>← All examples</a>
    <p class="eyebrow">LEARN BY CHANGING</p>
    <h1>Make the line yours.</h1>
    <p>Five points. Two scales. Three ways to connect them. Explore the geometry and take the working code with you.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="live-example" aria-label="Interactive line example">
    <LiveLine client:load noMeta embeddedEditor={import.meta.env.PUBLIC_EMBED_EDITOR !== 'false'} sources={lineSources} templateUrl={sitePath('/downloads/line-template.json')} />
    <noscript><p>This example needs JavaScript for its controls. <a href={sitePath('/docs/#quick-start')}>Read the static quick start</a> or <a href={sitePath('/examples/#curves')}>compare the precomputed curves</a>.</p></noscript>
  </section>
  <section class="closing-callout">
    <h2>The pieces stay simple.</h2>
    <p>Scales map your values to coordinates. The line primitive connects the points. FoldKit keeps control state in the Model and applies changes through Messages.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/docs/#foldkit')}>Explore the architecture →</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .live-example { min-width: 0; }
  .live-example astro-island[ssr]::before { content: 'Preparing the live example…'; display: block; padding: 48px; border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); }
</style>
